{"Line 73 repeats the grantType null-check instead of checking rawTokenId, so rawTokenId == null can slip through and later be encoded as '...:null' instead of failing fast": 0.9791507720947266, "isAccessTokenId matcher has inverted logic - returns false when grant shortcut matches instead of when they do not match": 0.9819991588592529, "Test catches RuntimeException instead of the specific parsing exception, making the test pass on unrelated failures like IndexOutOfBoundsException or NullPointerException": 0.8157041668891907, "The decoder assumes a fixed 2+2+2 prefix but the factory never validates that grant shortcuts are exactly 2 characters, meaning custom grants can emit token IDs that later fail to decode": 0.9161510467529297, "The lazy refresh paths at Lines 106-137 bypass the one-time duplicate check, allowing a custom grant to overwrite an existing shortcut mapping at runtime": 0.8509191870689392, "isAccessTokenId matcher uses wrong substring indices - substring(3, 5) extracts characters at indices 3-4 ('ta') instead of the grant type which should be substring(4, 6)": 0.9857255220413208, "grantType field is captured once in constructor but setFormParams() can replace parameters later without updating it, making getGrantType() return stale data": 0.9633277654647827}